# Private-namespace members and their homes, one "DICT /name" per line.
# The dict-homes test asserts every pair still appears in data/*.ps: a
# member may gain company but may not move home or vanish. A feature
# that adds a member appends it here in the same commit, so the file
# is the running register of where interpreter machinery lives.
#
# A name here is the whole name. Five entries were once prefixes of a
# longer name and were satisfied by it -- /DATA by DATA_DIR, /GRAPHICS by
# GRAPHICS_LOADED, /initial by initial_ipos, /hodgman by
# hodgman-sutherland, /.xpost by the nine device class dictionaries --
# so they registered members that do not exist while the ones that do
# went unheld.
#
# A name here is also one the PostScript defines, not one a comment about
# it spells. /h was registered against the line of data/init.ps that
# writes an imaginary helper to show what the helper-call idiom looks
# like; nothing has ever defined a member of that name.
.gscratch /.pfdict
.gscratch /strokedict
.internaldict /.fillpoly
.internaldict /.fillrectgray
.internaldict /GRAPHICS_LOADED
.internaldict /QUIET
.internaldict /.=stringproc
.internaldict /.sysdictrelock
.internaldict /USEDRAWLINE
.privatedict /DATA_DIR
.privatedict /.error
.privatedict /.graphicsdict
.privatedict /.gstatetemplate
.privatedict /.hairhw
.privatedict /.hairrect
.privatedict /.imginterp
.privatedict /newnulldevice
.gscratch /.stencilcache
